WEBVTT

00:11.860 --> 00:14.240
Oh, it's you, Yumina.

00:17.690 --> 00:20.980
I wish this could last forever.

00:24.150 --> 00:25.430
<i>Hold on!</i>

00:25.430 --> 00:27.540
<i>What is Yumina doing here?</i>

00:28.030 --> 00:30.760
<i>I know went to bed by myself last night!</i>

00:30.760 --> 00:34.010
<i>Also, I've never slept 
with anyone else before!</i>

00:42.020 --> 00:44.440
Oh, Touya.

00:45.270 --> 00:46.980
Good morning.

00:46.980 --> 00:49.500
<i>She's cute like this, too!</i>

00:50.860 --> 00:52.110
Uh, I mean...

00:52.110 --> 00:53.940
What are you doing here, Yumina?

00:53.940 --> 00:58.910
My, there's nothing odd about a wife and 
husband sleeping in the same bed, you know.

00:58.910 --> 01:02.110
Uh, but we're not married yet, you know.

01:02.110 --> 01:03.940
Besides, lately,

01:03.940 --> 01:07.260
you've been all focused on the nation, 
and you haven't spent any time with me.

01:07.260 --> 01:09.420
So you owe me at least this much.

01:09.420 --> 01:11.670
<i>How much is "this much"'?!</i>

01:11.670 --> 01:14.280
It's almost time for breakfast.

01:14.280 --> 01:15.780
I'll go get ready.

01:17.260 --> 01:18.390
Huh?

01:24.490 --> 01:25.570
I'll get changed.

01:27.800 --> 01:31.880
Gather up your tears

01:31.880 --> 01:34.280
And release your unhindered light

01:34.280 --> 01:39.210
That shines like a diamond

01:39.210 --> 01:40.720
Don't worry, don't care

01:40.720 --> 01:43.760
Follow your heart

01:54.550 --> 02:00.810
Every time I spoke of my
dreams, they felt closed off

02:00.810 --> 02:07.120
Even that bird and that sky
seemed monochrome to me

02:07.120 --> 02:13.570
Yet you were there in my path,
your eyes brimming with strength

02:13.570 --> 02:20.250
Time then stopped, and deep within
my heart something began to stir

02:22.320 --> 02:26.330
Don't be afraid, and run forth

02:26.330 --> 02:28.700
If we only have one life to live

02:28.700 --> 02:35.010
Then be true to yourself,
so you don't regret it

02:35.010 --> 02:39.100
Gather up your tears

02:39.100 --> 02:41.480
And release your unhindered light

02:41.480 --> 02:46.500
That shines like a diamond

02:46.500 --> 02:47.970
Don't worry, don't care

02:47.970 --> 02:51.120
Follow your heart

02:57.030 --> 03:02.030
Episode 7

02:57.030 --> 03:02.030
The Hangar and Frame Gears

03:03.490 --> 03:05.510
That was so forward of Yumina-san.

03:05.510 --> 03:08.250
Five wives for one husband...

03:08.250 --> 03:10.910
You have a rough ride ahead.

03:11.270 --> 03:12.230
Master.

03:13.800 --> 03:17.230
I just received word from one 
of the birds we sent scouting.

03:17.230 --> 03:19.470
Oh, they found something already?

03:19.470 --> 03:23.970
They describe it as a pitch-black 
pyramid made from some unusual material.

03:23.970 --> 03:27.230
<i>That sounds similar to 
the Alchemy Ward's ruins.</i>

03:27.230 --> 03:29.350
<i>This might be a jackpot.</i>

03:29.350 --> 03:32.310
So where are these ruins?

03:34.450 --> 03:36.020
There you have it.

03:36.020 --> 03:39.110
So I know it's early, but 
I'm planning to go Babylon.

03:39.110 --> 03:41.950
The location is on the western 
side of the Kingdom of Sandora.

03:42.360 --> 03:45.410
The island is a lot smaller than Brunhild.

03:45.410 --> 03:48.060
So this will be the fourth Babylon?

03:48.060 --> 03:50.060
Yeah, if we're lucky.

03:50.060 --> 03:52.870
I hope it's either the Storehouse 
or the Hangar this time.

03:52.870 --> 03:55.060
The Library would be good, as well.

03:55.060 --> 03:57.480
I'd actually be more grateful if it was.

03:57.480 --> 04:00.490
I think it's probably the Tower.

04:00.490 --> 04:03.090
I think it's the Research Lab.

04:03.090 --> 04:05.800
Then I'll bet on the Rampart.

04:05.800 --> 04:08.940
Come on, let's not turn 
this into a betting pool.

04:08.940 --> 04:13.270
Ende also said it's only a matter of time 
before Advanced Phrase appear,

04:13.600 --> 04:16.290
so I hope we can obtain the Frame Gears soon.

04:17.600 --> 04:20.800
Please! Let it be the Hangar 
or the Storehouse!

04:25.610 --> 04:29.450
It looks like the ruin is straight ahead.

04:29.450 --> 04:32.970
Is there really no one living here?

04:32.970 --> 04:34.710
None that my search is showing.

04:34.710 --> 04:39.420
Maybe that just means there are that many 
animals and monsters roaming wild there.

04:40.630 --> 04:43.220
Looks like a strange one has already shown up.

04:49.470 --> 04:53.110
No, Paula, you don't need to fight.

05:02.140 --> 05:03.240
Here it comes!

05:06.740 --> 05:08.460
Entwine thus, Ice!

05:08.460 --> 05:11.390
Frozen Curse: Icebind!

05:14.910 --> 05:16.240
Here I go!

05:25.510 --> 05:27.520
Time to finish it!

05:32.350 --> 05:34.980
That wasn't a very impressive monster.

05:34.980 --> 05:37.290
It was around Green Rank, I'd say.

05:37.290 --> 05:39.740
It has a pretty tough hide, though.

05:39.740 --> 05:42.640
We might be able to use it to make something.

05:42.640 --> 05:44.820
Shall we take some home with us?

05:44.820 --> 05:47.720
There was no need for me to step in.

05:49.490 --> 05:51.160
But this time...

05:51.160 --> 05:53.210
Everyone, let's go!

05:53.210 --> 05:53.990
Aye!

05:53.990 --> 05:55.660
Th-This time...

05:57.860 --> 05:59.990
There! There!

05:58.540 --> 05:59.990
Piece of cake!

06:00.630 --> 06:03.880
As expected from us!

06:00.630 --> 06:03.880
Yeah. I can really count on you all.

06:21.630 --> 06:23.200
This is definitely it!

06:23.200 --> 06:25.160
A teleportation circle to Babylon!

06:25.690 --> 06:27.000
I found it.

06:27.000 --> 06:28.150
I'm teleporting now.

06:28.150 --> 06:29.420
Understood.

06:29.420 --> 06:30.610
Be careful.

06:40.900 --> 06:43.120
Oh, I'm here.

06:45.960 --> 06:47.290
What's that?

06:55.470 --> 06:57.180
Hey, that's dangerous!

06:57.180 --> 06:58.420
Not bad.

06:58.420 --> 07:02.150
You're the first to dodge 
my instant-kill attack.

07:02.550 --> 07:05.340
Though no one else has ever 
come here before, either!

07:07.230 --> 07:10.220
<i>So this girl is the administrator 
of this Babylon?</i>

07:10.220 --> 07:12.740
<i>She's tiny, though.</i>

07:13.400 --> 07:15.410
Uh, who are you?

07:15.410 --> 07:19.250
I am the administrator of 
this Babylon, Fredmonica!

07:20.120 --> 07:21.580
Call me Monica!

07:23.430 --> 07:24.550
And you are?

07:24.550 --> 07:27.380
Oh, I'm Mochizuki Touya.

07:27.380 --> 07:33.180
I'm the Master of... let's see... the Garden, 
the Workshop, and the Alchemy Ward.

07:33.180 --> 07:34.550
I see.

07:34.550 --> 07:37.640
So you've already obtained 
several Babylons, then.

07:38.040 --> 07:41.940
Then prove your strength to me!

07:43.400 --> 07:44.560
Slip!

07:49.390 --> 07:50.740
<i>I saw her panties.</i>

07:52.250 --> 07:53.700
Y-You saw, didn't you?

07:53.700 --> 07:55.450
Huh? Uh...

07:55.450 --> 07:57.880
I think you're a little young 
to be wearing black.

08:01.180 --> 08:02.500
...erase...

08:02.500 --> 08:03.210
Huh?

08:03.210 --> 08:05.980
I'll erase your memory!

08:05.980 --> 08:06.950
Shield.

08:10.780 --> 08:12.050
<i>I saw them again.</i>

08:15.190 --> 08:17.010
I can still see them.

08:17.010 --> 08:19.850
Damn it!

08:19.850 --> 08:21.270
I can still see them.

08:22.020 --> 08:23.480
I give up!

08:24.570 --> 08:26.940
Why do I feel so guilty?

08:26.940 --> 08:30.500
I now recognize you as compatible!

08:30.500 --> 08:32.510
And as of this moment, Unit #28,

08:32.510 --> 08:35.690
code name "Fredmonica," will be 
transferred to your command!

08:36.260 --> 08:37.880
Now help me up, Master!

08:44.580 --> 08:46.530
Registration complete!

08:46.530 --> 08:48.790
Master's genetic information recorded!

08:48.790 --> 08:53.010
Ownership of the Hangar is 
now transferred to Master!

08:53.010 --> 08:54.520
The Hangar?

08:55.550 --> 08:57.340
Yes! Bingo!

08:57.340 --> 08:58.390
Bingo?

08:58.390 --> 09:00.470
Hey, Monica! The Frame Gears!

09:00.470 --> 09:03.100
The Frame Gears are here, right?!

09:03.100 --> 09:04.940
Y-Yeah.

09:10.270 --> 09:13.060
This is awfully spacious, isn't it?

09:13.060 --> 09:14.540
Bet you're surprised, huh?

09:14.540 --> 09:17.720
Spatial Magic is used on 
the interior of the Hangar,

09:17.720 --> 09:20.000
so it's a lot bigger inside than it looks!

09:25.320 --> 09:27.040
Uh, want me to push it?

09:25.680 --> 09:27.040
Damn it... You little...

09:27.040 --> 09:28.250
You bastard!

09:29.080 --> 09:30.460
Whoa, whoa!

09:30.460 --> 09:32.430
You're too quick to snap!

09:39.970 --> 09:42.270
So this is a Frame Gear?!

09:42.270 --> 09:45.480
This is the original Frame Gear, 
so it's an old model.

09:45.480 --> 09:47.370
Hey, can I get in this?

09:47.370 --> 09:49.160
You can get in it all you want!

09:49.570 --> 09:51.270
It won't run, though.

09:52.950 --> 09:53.610
Huh?

09:53.610 --> 09:54.930
Why won't it run?

09:54.930 --> 09:56.080
Because it has no fuel.

09:56.080 --> 09:58.330
What does this thing use for fuel?! Gasoline?!

09:58.330 --> 09:59.570
Gasoline?

09:59.880 --> 10:02.680
This thing uses Ether Liquid for fuel!

10:02.680 --> 10:06.040
If I remember right, the administrator 
of the Research Lab can make it.

10:07.140 --> 10:10.500
So you're saying we have to find 
the Research Lab to make them run?!

10:11.370 --> 10:13.590
D-Don't be disappointed, Master!

10:13.590 --> 10:16.550
It's possible that Flora might know how!

10:17.240 --> 10:18.130
Huh?

10:18.820 --> 10:20.590
Ether Liquid?

10:20.970 --> 10:23.310
It's not impossible to make.

10:23.310 --> 10:25.000
All right!

10:25.000 --> 10:28.060
Though what I can make here will be inferior

10:28.060 --> 10:30.460
to what the Research Lab 
administrator could make.

10:30.460 --> 10:31.630
That's no problem!

10:31.630 --> 10:33.860
Now we can operate the Frame Gears!

10:33.860 --> 10:35.030
Good for you.

10:35.030 --> 10:37.860
So, do you have any Ether Ore?

10:38.690 --> 10:41.570
Huh? Ether Ore?

10:41.570 --> 10:47.230
It's an ore with the ability to amplify, 
store, and release magic energy.

10:47.230 --> 10:49.670
We would need some about this large.

10:49.670 --> 10:54.500
Um, are you talking about spellstones?

10:56.650 --> 10:58.370
There's no doubt.

10:58.370 --> 11:00.760
These are Ether Ores.

11:00.760 --> 11:02.520
So, problem solved?!

11:05.050 --> 11:07.130
What's wrong, everyone?

11:07.780 --> 11:09.770
Well, I mean...

11:09.770 --> 11:13.400
To be blunt, there aren't 
any spellstones that large.

11:13.400 --> 11:14.640
Huh?

11:14.640 --> 11:17.360
Spellstones are incredibly precious items.

11:17.810 --> 11:20.320
If there was a spellstone that large...

11:20.320 --> 11:22.450
You wouldn't be able to put a price on it.

11:22.450 --> 11:24.160
You're kidding me!

11:24.160 --> 11:27.580
Could we not search for one 
using your smartphone, Touya-dono?

11:27.580 --> 11:28.580
Huh?

11:28.580 --> 11:29.560
Oh!

11:29.960 --> 11:31.100
Search.

11:31.100 --> 11:33.680
A spellstone bigger than 30cm.

11:34.980 --> 11:36.700
Oh, look at this!

11:36.700 --> 11:38.300
There's one in Brunhild, too!

11:38.300 --> 11:39.750
You're right!

11:39.750 --> 11:43.050
All right! Then our next step 
is mining spellstones!

11:49.810 --> 11:51.440
How's this?!

11:51.440 --> 11:54.150
Oh, my. It's rather big.

11:54.600 --> 11:57.080
Half of this should be plenty.

11:58.460 --> 12:01.650
Just a month until the 
Ether Liquid is complete...

12:03.060 --> 12:04.570
I can't wait!

12:04.960 --> 12:07.240
Oh? Is that you, Master?

12:08.070 --> 12:09.710
What are you two up to?

12:09.710 --> 12:14.020
It has been 5,000 years, so I figured 
we should do some light maintenance.

12:14.020 --> 12:19.070
The Hangar comes equipped with magic 
that prevents corrosion and deterioration,

12:19.070 --> 12:21.350
but dust and the like can still build up.

12:21.350 --> 12:23.970
I told you, they ain't covered in dust!

12:23.970 --> 12:26.050
I've been taking proper care of them!

12:26.860 --> 12:28.030
Have you really?

12:28.030 --> 12:29.320
Oh, right, Master!

12:29.320 --> 12:31.600
Would you like to try 
sitting in the pilot seat?

12:31.600 --> 12:33.930
Really?! Can I?!

12:43.370 --> 12:45.320
Yeah, not bad.

12:45.320 --> 12:48.170
Once you understand the 
basic motions for piloting it,

12:48.170 --> 12:50.000
the rest is just practice.

12:50.000 --> 12:53.600
The unit itself handles all the detailed 
assistance and adjustments

12:53.600 --> 12:55.670
by reading the pilot's mind.

12:55.980 --> 12:59.880
Though that also means a lot is dependent 
on the pilot's thoughts and experience,

12:59.880 --> 13:01.930
so a veteran warrior would be even stronger,

13:01.930 --> 13:05.010
while those who aren't would 
only be able to pilot it so well.

13:05.010 --> 13:07.110
I see...

13:07.110 --> 13:10.110
Oh, man, I can't wait to try piloting it.

13:10.110 --> 13:12.470
It'll take time to get used to it, too.

13:12.470 --> 13:14.310
I had a feeling this might happen!

13:14.310 --> 13:19.520
So I actually made you something in secret!

13:20.030 --> 13:25.610
This is the Frame Unit, a simulation 
system for training with Frame Gears!

13:25.610 --> 13:28.510
Is it one of those things that 
provides a simulated experience?

13:28.510 --> 13:29.650
It is!

13:29.650 --> 13:32.660
And it operates solely on magic power!

13:58.230 --> 14:00.500
<i>How does it feel to pilot one?</i>

14:00.500 --> 14:03.070
Great! It pretty much moves as I will it to!

14:16.870 --> 14:17.830
What now?

14:17.830 --> 14:20.790
<i>Looks like you're getting used to it, Master!</i>

14:20.790 --> 14:23.880
Now I'll teach you how to 
pilot it in actual combat!

14:27.720 --> 14:29.220
Now I get it.

14:29.220 --> 14:32.220
The second unit was for 
communication and competition.

14:32.630 --> 14:35.480
All right! Let's go!

14:36.600 --> 14:38.440
I'll get you!

14:39.290 --> 14:41.100
There, there, there!

14:41.570 --> 14:43.440
D-Don't look!

14:45.400 --> 14:47.490
We can use these as much as we want?!

14:47.490 --> 14:50.110
That's exactly why I had 
the Workshop make copies.

14:50.410 --> 14:52.410
Play around with them 
whenever you're free.

14:52.410 --> 14:55.390
<i>Eventually, we'll make them available 
to everyone in the castle</i>

14:55.390 --> 14:56.790
<i>and have them practice, as well.</i>

14:57.360 --> 15:00.750
<i>During that time, we'll work on mass 
production of actual Frame Gear units.</i>

15:01.190 --> 15:03.700
<i>Though that will still mean only one a day.</i>

15:03.700 --> 15:07.670
<i>But in several months' time, we should 
have enough for everyone in the castle.</i>

15:07.670 --> 15:08.620
<i>Good.</i>

15:08.620 --> 15:12.640
<i>Now we should be prepared if any 
standard or more powerful Phrase attack.</i>

15:12.640 --> 15:14.100
Touya!

15:14.100 --> 15:17.680
<i>I know! "Mass-Produced Frame Gear" 
is a pretty boring name.</i>

15:17.680 --> 15:20.890
<i>So let's call them Chevaliers, 
the word for knights!</i>

15:22.880 --> 15:24.140
Sue?

15:24.730 --> 15:28.150
Touya! Make me your wife, too!

15:28.150 --> 15:29.420
Let's get married!

15:29.420 --> 15:30.480
What?!

15:30.480 --> 15:32.600
You like younger women, right?

15:33.850 --> 15:35.400
Who told you that?

15:35.400 --> 15:37.620
I heard it from your maid, Cesca!

15:37.620 --> 15:39.950
And I'm the youngest one so far!

15:39.950 --> 15:41.750
So there's no issue!

15:40.410 --> 15:43.800
Young lady, that's enough.

15:43.800 --> 15:46.210
You're troubling His Royal Highness.

15:46.210 --> 15:49.410
What is going on here, Leim-san?

15:49.410 --> 15:51.420
I'm not following the conversation.

15:51.880 --> 15:56.140
The truth is, Lady Sushie has received 
an offer for an arranged marriage.

15:56.760 --> 15:57.640
Huh?

15:58.100 --> 16:00.810
I won't marry anyone other than Touya!

16:00.810 --> 16:02.190
I refuse!

16:02.560 --> 16:04.900
So who would be her partner?

16:04.900 --> 16:08.610
His Highness Zabune, the first 
prince of Linhea Kingdom.

16:08.610 --> 16:13.160
The first prince? That would 
make him the future king, right?

16:13.550 --> 16:15.120
That doesn't sound like a bad arrangement.

16:15.120 --> 16:16.500
How doesn't it?!

16:16.500 --> 16:19.390
I refuse to wed some mysterious man!

16:19.390 --> 16:20.080
Indeed.

16:20.080 --> 16:21.850
Huh? You too, Leim-san?

16:22.360 --> 16:24.920
Personally, I'm opposed to it.

16:24.920 --> 16:29.080
First of all, Prince Zabune 
has a bad reputation.

16:29.480 --> 16:31.760
Especially in his relationships with women.

16:32.140 --> 16:34.690
There are countless noble 
ladies and city girls

16:34.690 --> 16:38.960
who have been brought to tears 
by his violence and awful treatment,

16:38.960 --> 16:41.370
and rumor has it that is 
why he still hasn't been

16:41.370 --> 16:44.470
able to succeed the throne
 despite being well past 30.

16:44.470 --> 16:45.190
Hey!

16:45.190 --> 16:46.820
W-W-Wait a minute!

16:46.820 --> 16:48.270
He's over 30?!

16:48.270 --> 16:49.900
Their ages are that far apart?!

16:49.900 --> 16:51.150
That's right!

16:51.150 --> 16:57.180
So, what? Are they just getting engaged for 
now, and then marrying after Sue is older?

16:57.180 --> 16:58.460
No.

16:58.460 --> 17:01.750
He wants to marry her right away.

17:01.750 --> 17:06.250
He claims he fell in love 
with her at the social party.

17:06.250 --> 17:08.080
I refuse!

17:08.570 --> 17:12.480
So Touya, please! Take me!

17:12.480 --> 17:15.060
You don't have to treat me 
the same as my sister Yumina!

17:15.060 --> 17:17.760
Just keeping me at your side would be enough!

17:19.430 --> 17:21.720
Is that too much, Touya?

17:26.220 --> 17:30.190
I'm also opposed to you marrying 
a stupid prince like that.

17:31.230 --> 17:32.150
Touya!

17:32.150 --> 17:35.380
<i>But this is a problem between nations,</i>

17:35.380 --> 17:38.660
<i>so I don't think it's something 
I can resolve at my own discretion.</i>

17:39.280 --> 17:41.330
<i>I guess I'll consult with the others.</i>

17:41.330 --> 17:43.930
I don't see any issue with her marrying you.

17:43.930 --> 17:45.310
Seems past due, really.

17:45.310 --> 17:47.430
I don't think it's a problem, either.

17:47.430 --> 17:51.190
I kind of had a feeling that 
it would turn out this way.

17:51.190 --> 17:53.550
I'm happy to have more companions.

17:54.830 --> 17:58.760
W-Well, setting that topic aside for now,

17:58.760 --> 18:02.670
the question is how to refuse 
Prince Zabune's marriage proposal.

18:02.670 --> 18:06.850
I can just turn him down by telling 
him I'm going to be Touya's bride.

18:06.850 --> 18:11.050
That could still cause some problems.

18:11.050 --> 18:15.040
I've heard that Prince Zabune 
is quite vindictive.

18:15.040 --> 18:19.100
Worst case, he could sever all relations 
between his nation and ours.

18:20.070 --> 18:22.620
I can't cause trouble for others...

18:23.320 --> 18:25.500
If only there was some way that would work...

18:28.760 --> 18:32.780
It would solve everything if we just 
crushed the life out of that prince.

18:32.780 --> 18:34.360
That's violent.

18:34.360 --> 18:38.510
A stupid prince acting that selfishly 
at his age is doing no one any good.

18:38.510 --> 18:42.070
A loathsome, perverted pedophile 
in his thirties who toys with women

18:42.070 --> 18:44.560
should be put out of his misery quickly.

18:44.560 --> 18:46.090
You're sure letting him have it!

18:46.090 --> 18:47.270
How do you plan to kill him?!

18:47.270 --> 18:49.870
I would manufacture a sniper rifle.

18:50.170 --> 18:52.570
A little potassium cyanide 
and he'd be out like a light.

18:52.940 --> 18:55.230
I just need one blow with my pipe wrench!

18:55.760 --> 18:58.740
Well, setting these idiots aside...

18:58.740 --> 19:01.570
At any rate, let's start by visiting the duke.

19:01.570 --> 19:05.350
We can tell him how Sue feels and have 
him try to think of something, too.

19:05.350 --> 19:07.850
Maybe there's something we can do together.

19:10.480 --> 19:13.750
I've been quite troubled 
by this problem, as well.

19:14.120 --> 19:18.340
If you were to agree to marry Sue, 
I would at least have some options...

19:18.340 --> 19:20.550
And what would happen in that case?

19:20.550 --> 19:24.380
All of that stupid prince's resentment 
would be turned toward Brunhild.

19:24.380 --> 19:25.930
That's mean!

19:27.070 --> 19:29.690
Getting back to this stupid prince...

19:29.690 --> 19:31.410
If he has such a bad reputation,

19:31.410 --> 19:34.480
the question is why he hasn't been 
expelled from the royal family.

19:34.480 --> 19:37.970
It's the power of Wardack, 
the Prime Minister of Linhea.

19:37.970 --> 19:42.110
It's no understatement to claim that 
man holds all the authority in Linhea.

19:42.110 --> 19:44.870
Rumor has it their king is just a figurehead.

19:44.870 --> 19:47.450
Just who is this prime minister?

19:47.450 --> 19:52.920
Wardack is from the same family as 
Queen Dacia, Prince Zabune's mother.

19:52.920 --> 19:55.630
He uses that status to get away 
with whatever he pleases.

19:56.160 --> 19:59.470
I hear the only decent person in that 
royal family is the second prince.

19:59.470 --> 20:02.550
Huh? There's another prince 
aside from this stupid one?

20:02.550 --> 20:04.860
He's a concubine's son, though.

20:04.860 --> 20:09.660
Apparently he's been forced to 
live away from the palace in shame,

20:09.660 --> 20:12.270
but I hear he's a man 
of quite good character.

20:12.270 --> 20:14.260
If he's from a different mother,

20:14.260 --> 20:16.980
that means he doesn't 
share Wardack's bloodline.

20:16.980 --> 20:21.050
However, the second prince's mother 
is kept isolated due to illness,

20:21.050 --> 20:22.960
and she has no backing.

20:22.960 --> 20:27.180
Apparently, all that prince can do 
is just barely keep her alive.

20:27.560 --> 20:29.200
That's tragic.

20:31.540 --> 20:35.920
Master, the emissary from Linhea has arrived.

20:36.320 --> 20:38.440
I guess they ran out of patience.

20:38.790 --> 20:40.380
All right, I've made up my mind.

20:40.750 --> 20:42.840
I'll formally decline.

20:42.840 --> 20:45.180
Okay, then, I'll be going—

20:47.190 --> 20:47.960
Huh?

20:48.640 --> 20:53.640
<b>Anxious</b>

20:48.640 --> 20:53.640
<b>Anxious</b>

20:48.640 --> 20:53.640
Anxious... Teary...

20:54.100 --> 20:56.090
Your Grace, Duke Ortlinde.

20:56.530 --> 20:59.360
Please pardon the interruption, 
but I have come to receive your answer

20:59.360 --> 21:01.480
regarding the recent proposal.

21:01.820 --> 21:04.400
Thank you for coming all this way.

21:05.140 --> 21:09.680
To get to the point, while we are truly 
honored by your gracious proposal,

21:09.680 --> 21:11.240
I will have to decline.

21:14.510 --> 21:17.080
Might I inquire the reason?

21:17.470 --> 21:21.420
The truth is, my daughter has 
already settled on another man to wed.

21:21.420 --> 21:22.280
Huh?!

21:21.710 --> 21:23.490
May I ask who he is?

21:24.420 --> 21:25.880
This man here.

21:25.880 --> 21:30.470
His Royal Highness, the Grand Duke of 
the Duchy of Brunhild, Mochizuki Touya.

21:30.470 --> 21:33.610
This man is the Grand Duke 
of the Duchy of Brunhild?!

21:35.920 --> 21:38.520
Oh, um, you don't need to do that for me.

21:38.900 --> 21:42.340
I never thought I would be able to 
meet Your Royal Highness here.

21:42.340 --> 21:43.610
I give my thanks to God!

21:43.610 --> 21:44.940
No, no, no...

21:44.940 --> 21:49.320
I have heard your achievements 
spoken of in many circles.

21:49.320 --> 21:51.330
Pardon me for asking,

21:51.330 --> 21:54.830
but is it true that you can 
use teleportation magic?

21:54.830 --> 21:55.460
Huh?

21:55.460 --> 21:57.960
Oh, yes, I can use it.

21:57.960 --> 21:59.220
Oh!

21:59.220 --> 22:00.150
In that case...

22:00.150 --> 22:03.190
In that case, please! 
Please save my mother!

22:03.190 --> 22:05.820
Huh? H-Hold on a minute!

22:05.820 --> 22:08.590
Could you explain things from the beginning?

22:08.590 --> 22:09.660
Yes.

22:10.180 --> 22:13.460
My name is Cloud Zeph Linhea.

22:13.460 --> 22:16.610
I am the second prince of Linhea Kingdom.

22:17.740 --> 22:18.820
Huh?!
